IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cvp-types`

-- Commonwealth Volunteers Protection Act 2003 (Cth) — THE RULES AND THE
-- TOP-LEVEL GOAL. The volunteer asks: "Am I protected from civil liability
-- for what I did as a volunteer, and if not me, who bears it?"

§ `Rules`

-- s 4(2): no remuneration beyond reasonable expenses, or less than the
-- prescribed amount, and not under a court order. s 4(3): the usual
-- employer's pay continues and nothing else, the work is of a kind usually
-- done unpaid (or low-paid), and not under a court order.
@ref s 4(2)-(3)
@export Did I do the work on a voluntary basis under s 4(2)-(3) of the Commonwealth Volunteers Protection Act 2003 (Cth)? Yes if I received nothing but reasonable expenses (or less than the prescribed amount), or my usual employer kept paying me and the work is of a kind usually done unpaid; and not under a court order. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`  @desc How I was paid, the kind of work, and any court order
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `on a voluntary basis` v IF
        NOT (v's `under a court order`)
    AND CONSIDER v's `how I was paid`
        WHEN `nothing but reasonable expenses`     THEN TRUE
        WHEN `less than the prescribed amount`     THEN TRUE
        WHEN `my usual pay from my employer only`  THEN v's `the work is usually done unpaid`
        WHEN `more than that`                      THEN FALSE

GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `for the Commonwealth or an authority` v IF
    NOT (v's `the work was for` EQUALS `someone else`)

-- s 6(1): "An individual does not incur civil liability for anything that
-- the individual has done in good faith in doing work for the Commonwealth
-- or a Commonwealth authority if it is work: (a) done ... on a voluntary
-- basis; and (b) organised by" it. (2): not CTP-insured liability or
-- defamation; (3): not if significantly impaired by a recreational drug;
-- (4): not if knowingly outside authority or contrary to instructions.
-- s 5: only for things done after commencement.
@ref ss 5, 6
@export Am I protected from civil liability for what I did as a volunteer, under s 6 of the Commonwealth Volunteers Protection Act 2003 (Cth)? Yes if I did it in good faith, after the Act commenced, in work for the Commonwealth or a Commonwealth authority that I did on a voluntary basis and that it organised; but not for liability covered by compulsory third-party motor insurance or for defamation, not if a recreational drug (including alcohol) significantly impaired my ability, and not if I knowingly acted outside the authorised activities or against instructions. DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`  @desc The work, how I was paid, what I did, and the kind of liability
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am protected under s 6` v IF
        v's `done after the Act commenced`
    AND `for the Commonwealth or an authority` v
    AND v's `done in good faith`
    AND `on a voluntary basis` v
    AND v's `organised by them`
    AND v's `the liability` EQUALS `another civil liability`
    AND NOT (v's `significantly impaired by a recreational drug`)
    AND NOT (v's `knowingly outside the authorised activities`)
    AND NOT (v's `knowingly contrary to instructions`)

-- s 7(1): the Commonwealth or the authority "incurs any civil liability that
-- an individual would, except for section 6, incur"; (2): not an authority
-- already protected by another Act.
@ref s 7
@export Who bears the civil liability for what I did as a volunteer, under s 7 of the Commonwealth Volunteers Protection Act 2003 (Cth)? The Commonwealth or the authority, where s 6 protects me; no one under this Act where another Act protects the authority; otherwise I do (this Act does not take it from me). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`  @desc The volunteer facts
GIVETH A `Who bears the liability`
`who bears the liability for` v MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`for the Commonwealth or an authority` v)   THEN `this Act does not apply`
        IF NOT (v's `done after the Act commenced`)          THEN `this Act does not apply`
        IF NOT (`I am protected under s 6` v)                THEN `I do`
        IF     v's `the work was for` EQUALS `a Commonwealth authority`
           AND v's `another Act protects the authority`      THEN `no one under this Act: the authority's own protection applies`
        OTHERWISE                                                 `the Commonwealth or the authority`

-- s 8: if asked to assist in a claim about a liability the Commonwealth or
-- authority may incur or incurs under s 7, "the individual must comply".
@ref s 8
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I must assist for` v IF
        v's `asked to assist`
    AND `who bears the liability for` v EQUALS `the Commonwealth or the authority`

-- s 9: an indemnity given by the individual against a liability the
-- Commonwealth or authority incurs under this Act "has no effect".
@ref s 9
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an indemnity I gave has effect for` v IF
    NOT (`who bears the liability for` v EQUALS `the Commonwealth or the authority`)

§ `The top-level goal`

@ref ss 4-9
@export default The volunteer's position under the Commonwealth Volunteers Protection Act 2003 (Cth): whether the work was done on a voluntary basis (s 4), whether I am protected from civil liability (s 6), who bears the liability (s 7), whether I must assist in defending the claim when asked (s 8), and whether an indemnity I gave against the Commonwealth's liability has effect (s 9). DRAFT, not reviewed by an Australian lawyer.
GIVEN v IS A `Volunteer case`  @desc The work, how I was paid, what I did, the kind of liability, and any request to assist
GIVETH A `Volunteer position`
`the volunteer position for` v MEANS
    `Volunteer position` WITH
        `voluntary basis`                               IS `on a voluntary basis` v
        `I am protected`                                IS `I am protected under s 6` v
        `who bears it`                                  IS `who bears the liability for` v
        `I must assist`                                 IS `I must assist for` v
        `my indemnity has effect`                       IS `an indemnity I gave has effect for` v
